{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02535",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.2,
      "end_seconds": 7.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.03,
      "end_seconds": 13.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.07,
      "end_seconds": 19.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.5,
      "end_seconds": 23.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 27.54,
      "end_seconds": 32.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Right, we came because of a widespread rash with fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.18,
      "end_seconds": 39.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Did it come on recently? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.89,
      "end_seconds": 47.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "It's been like this since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.42,
      "end_seconds": 58.16,
      "duration_seconds": 9.74,
      "text": "Alright, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.57,
      "end_seconds": 69.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "It's on and off. I'd call it mild. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.93,
      "end_seconds": 78.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "I mean, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 78.82,
      "end_seconds": 83.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.15,
      "end_seconds": 87.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.22,
      "end_seconds": 93.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Has there been a recent new medicine too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.82,
      "end_seconds": 97.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Erm, yes, about the same, two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.35,
      "end_seconds": 102.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "So, what about swollen face, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.98,
      "end_seconds": 107.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Yes, I have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.42,
      "end_seconds": 112.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "So, is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.35,
      "end_seconds": 116.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "It's on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.67,
      "end_seconds": 120.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Any blisters, breathing difficulty or mouth sores?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.6,
      "end_seconds": 133.86,
      "duration_seconds": 11.26,
      "text": "No, no blisters, no breathing difficulty, no mouth sores. I did have swollen glands at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.93,
      "end_seconds": 138.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.78,
      "end_seconds": 145.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.88,
      "end_seconds": 149.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.75,
      "end_seconds": 156.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol. My mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.11,
      "end_seconds": 159.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.3,
      "end_seconds": 164.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.47,
      "end_seconds": 169.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.29,
      "end_seconds": 173.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.82,
      "end_seconds": 177.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.26,
      "end_seconds": 183.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "I've had high cholesterol, yes. Thin bones, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.23,
      "end_seconds": 186.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Okay, what else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.64,
      "end_seconds": 200.43,
      "duration_seconds": 11.79,
      "text": "I have an irregular heartbeat, for two years. I, I have gout, for five years. Heart disease, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.51,
      "end_seconds": 214.37,
      "duration_seconds": 11.86,
      "text": "Right, right. Yes, high cholesterol and thin bones are known to us, good to have that clear. Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.15,
      "end_seconds": 220.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "It's atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.4,
      "end_seconds": 231.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.02,
      "text": "Mm, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.92,
      "end_seconds": 235.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.97,
      "end_seconds": 246.96,
      "duration_seconds": 10.99,
      "text": "For my bones, I believe. My daughter sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Apixaban, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.79,
      "end_seconds": 249.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.79,
      "end_seconds": 257.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "5 milligrams. I take allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day for the gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 257.99,
      "end_seconds": 265.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "It's meant to be once a day, though I don't see he take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.84,
      "end_seconds": 271.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.51,
      "end_seconds": 276.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 277.9,
      "end_seconds": 290.75,
      "duration_seconds": 12.85,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. SpO2 95 percent on room air, pulse is 94 beats a minute, respiratory rate 18, temp 38.8 degrees, pressure 114 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.54,
      "end_seconds": 292.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.44,
      "end_seconds": 298.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.04,
      "end_seconds": 313.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.66,
      "end_seconds": 318.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Okay, tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.44,
      "end_seconds": 335.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "There is a widespread red rash, facial swelling, and your temperature is high with enlarged glands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.57,
      "end_seconds": 337.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.63,
      "end_seconds": 344.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.88,
      "end_seconds": 367.81,
      "duration_seconds": 13.93,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: It's hard to say. A severe drug reaction is one possibility and a viral rash another, and I'd rather not commit yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.43,
      "end_seconds": 370.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.29,
      "end_seconds": 407.58,
      "duration_seconds": 35.29,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a severe drug reaction, and we'll know more once the urgent blood tests is back. I want urgent blood tests done, that's for severe drug reaction. I'll start you on prednisolone, 40 milligrams, once a day, until review. That should help with severe drug reaction. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Stop the allopurinol now and you need admission."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.35,
      "end_seconds": 413.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 415.36,
      "end_seconds": 417.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}